## 🔹 Key Takeaway

Today I understood that **Amazon S3 stores static website content, while CloudFront distributes that content efficiently through AWS's edge network**.

The overall concept I learned was:

```text
User
  ↓
CloudFront
  ↓
Nearest Edge Location
  ↓
Cache
  ↓
S3 Origin (if required)
```

CloudFront therefore acts as the **delivery and caching layer between users and the origin**, helping applications deliver content with lower latency and better performance.
